1. Objective

Provide a reproducible, testable, and modular framework for detecting gravitational anomalies and evaluating localized antigravity coupling stability using Hamiltonian dynamics, structural tensegrity analysis, and timeline‑based regime classification.

2. System Architecture Overview

Layer 1 — Astrophysical Intake

Required data streams:

Stellar kinematics (GAIA‑like)

CMB anisotropy tensor fields

Quasar drift time‑series

Cosmic ray flux

Validation modules:

Tensor consistency check

Field alignment check

Statistical validity check

Output:

Cleaned tensor field (T_{\mu\nu}(x))

Initial conditions for particle states (r_i(0), p_i(0))

Layer 2 — Hamiltonian Dynamics Core

Hamiltonian:

[ H = \sum_i \left( \frac{p_i^2}{2m_i} + V(r_i) \right)

\sum_{i < j} \frac{G m_i m_j}{r_{ij}}

\Lambda \sum_i r_i^2 ]

Coupling constants:

[ \alpha = \frac{1}{4\pi \epsilon_0}, \quad \beta = \frac{G}{c^4}, \quad \gamma = \frac{1}{2\omega_0^2} ]

Evolution:

[ \dot{r}_i = \frac{p_i}{m_i}, \quad \dot{p}_i = -\frac{\partial H}{\partial r_i} ]

Integrator requirement:

Symplectic (Leapfrog / Verlet)

Fixed timestep (\Delta t)

Stability‑checked force evaluation

Layer 3 — Structural Geometry & Tensegrity

Node set: particle positions (r_i)

Edge set: structural links ((i,j))

Rest lengths: (L_{ij})

Stiffness coefficients: (k_{ij})

Stress functional:

[ S_{\text{geom}} = \sum_{(i,j)} k_{ij}^2 (r_{ij} - L_{ij})^2 ]

Lab‑required outputs:

Stress magnitude

Stress derivative

Structural failure flags

Geometry integrity score

Layer 4 — Event‑Drift Timeline Classification

Regime classification based on:

Acceleration magnitude

Stress trend

Curvature proxy from (T_{\mu\nu})

Labels:

Warped — unstable curvature + rising stress

Stable — bounded stress + consistent dynamics

Accelerating — monotonic increase in anomaly strength

